  9751	    - the export writes its key and folder only after every store passed its check.
  9752	  - **Now:** 44 tests; 35 mutants and 5 controls, all as predicted, each mutant failing its own assertion.
  9753	- **Card form check after the round-3 card changes** (D673; `stage0/blinding-check-codex-3.md`, `-4.md`):
  9754	  - Round 3 named one form element: a third annotation form that the answer step appends to a rung condition. The filter is now the
  9755	    closed set of `ladder_step.py`'s three suffixes; of 484 stored conditions, none is left annotated.
  9756	  - Round 4 named only content: the number of rungs, the number of themes and the size of the library. The check is closed.
  9757	- **Round 4.**
  9758	  - **Readers' verdicts on the reading tools:** the Claude reader said "ready to read". Codex named three more points, all fixed:
  9759	    - the scorer takes each card's guardrail, covering and type marks from the verified deck key, and refuses readings that differ.
  9760	      Codex had flipped a loss to a lead by changing six flags in memory;
  9761	    - the 72-hour timing needs a complete attempt log: its line count must equal the ledger's attempts plus refusals, its charges must
  9762	      sum to the spend, and nothing may still be reserved. A missing or short log leaves the timing "not established", and the draw is
  9763	      not eligible. On slice 2: 156 of 156 and 79 of 79;
  9764	    - theme context on the card keeps the update marker and lists each theme's numbered possible answers. 29 of 52 stored theme reasons
  9765	      cite another rung.
  9766	  - **Also fixed:**
  9767	    - the card refuses a request whose evidence count it cannot read in full;
  9768	    - eligibility resolves the run root before it compares paths.
  9769	  - **Totals:** 47 tests; 39 mutants and 5 controls, all as predicted. 125 answered cards are built on all 12 stored stores of both
  9770	    systems without a refusal.
  9771	  - **The §1.6 design moved to v2 (`DESIGN-1.6.md`) on both readers' Part B:**
  9772	    - every store is taken from `run.json` and fingerprinted;
  9773	    - the release status is printed beside the verdict;
  9774	    - Step 2 line 1 uses the neutral labelling question, a generator-miss audit, and labels frozen before retrieval is read;
  9775	    - line 3 is a paired test that varies grouping alone, against an independent detail key;
  9776	    - D431 records its substitution and its comparability rule;
  9777	    - every printed-beside item has its tool.
     1	# The §1.6 tools: what D665 prints beside the verdict (design v2, before any output is read; D672)
     2	
     3	Governing text:
     4	- `RUN-PLAN-v12.md` §1.6;
     5	- `stage0/verdict-rule.json`: `hard_checks` and `printed_beside`.
     6	
     7	The ruler and the frozen instruments do not move (D674). Every reader is a closed session (`census/census_readers.run`), one per
     8	family, with memories off (D661).
     9	
    10	v2 answers round 4's Part B: Codex in `tools-review-codex-4.md`, and the Claude reader summarised in D675.
    11	
    12	## 0. Inputs, release status and the report
    13	
    14	- **Stores.**
    15	  - Every tool reads a draw's components from its `run.json`: `components[c]['folder']`, so `step1-redo` or `step2-redo` after a D449
    16	    redo, and the judge's completed attempt (`mapping.store_paths`).
    17	  - `eligibility.py` fingerprints every file a tool reads: the judge or old store, `step1/trace.sqlite`, `step2/decisions.json` and
    18	    `library.json`, and each pass's ladder `outcomes.jsonl`.
    19	  - Each tool refuses a file whose sha256 differs.
    20	- **Release status sits beside the verdict and does not replace it.**
    21	  - `score_comparison` gives the verdict (invalid / too small / lead / loss / no winner).
    22	  - The report adds "release: clear", or "release blocked: <check>" for any hard check that failed or was not measured (D665: "a release
    23	    blocker reported with the verdict").
    24	- **A hard check that is not measured cannot clear release.**
    25	  - The frozen rule says this of Step 2's lines. This design reads it the same way for D400's code parts, whose own accounting marks a
    26	    line "not measured" below 3 company-figure theses or 20 laddered theses.
    27	  - This is a reading to settle in the council and record before any output; it is the cautious, reversible course.
    28	- **Printed beside, each from its tool:**
    29	
    30	| Item | Tool | Source |
    31	|---|---|---|
    32	| D428's limits beside the guardrails | `score_comparison.beside` | The new system's figure share against 12.7% to 14.4%, its yes/no share against 5%, as D428 states them |
    33	| Sign test and interval (illustrative) | `score_comparison.beside` | Matters served by exactly one system: two-sided binomial p on a against b, and the Wilson 95% interval for a/(a+b), labelled illustrative |
    34	| Company-figure subgroup a, b, N | `score_comparison.beside` | Built |
    35	| Days from first source to opening | `score_comparison.beside` | For each matter a system serves: the matter's `first_day` (`matters.json`) to the earliest opening day of a covering question, per draw |
    36	| Floors | `score_comparison.beside` | §4 |
    37	| D400 reader lines, D400 code parts | §1 | |
    38	| Step 2's three lines | §2 | |
    39	| D431's 07-14 reading | §3 | |
    40	| 37 bulk-viewer articles excluded; 2 split matter pairs kept apart | report text | D669 and D671 records |
    41	
    42	## 1. D400, all three passes
    43	
    44	- **Code parts** (`d400_code_check.py`): Stage A's accounting, line 6, on each new draw's three ladder passes. The ladder folder comes
    45	  from `run.json`.
    46	  - A skipped ladder component (no question opened) is "not measured".
    47	  - "Figure ranges meet end to end" is enforced at the write (`ladder_step.check_answer`).
    48	- **Reader lines 1–5:** Stage A's reading, unchanged, run per draw. `collect_readings.py` reads one ladder folder and its packet files:
    49	  `build_reader_packets.py <key> --run <ladder folder>=<cases.json> --readers <draw's reader folder>`, then
    50	  `collect_readings.py rows | disputes | report` on that folder.
    51	
    52	## 2. Step 2's three lines on draw new-1 (hard)
    53	
    54	Inputs: new-1's Step 1 trace, its `decisions.json` and its `library.json`. The seed is 20261117 plus the line's number.
    55	
    56	**Line 1, search.**
    57	- **Sample:** records drawn at random in three equal article strata (by forward position).
    58	- **Candidates:** earlier records only, in forward order, from two routes that do not use Step 2's embeddings:
    59	  - entity-wide word overlap, top 10 (`retrieve.py` R0e);
    60	  - the same original party within 3 days.
    61	- **Labels:** two readers, one per family, answer the neutral relation question of the Step 2 reference labelling
    62	  (`poc/data/step2-validation-2026-11-07/v2-prompt-*.md`, question 1: the relation of the later record to the earlier, with no claim that
    63	  the system filed it). A third reader settles disagreements.
    64	- **Generator-miss audit (Step 2 log §1):** for each sampled record, 5 random earlier records of the same entity that neither route
    65	  returned are labelled the same way. A same-statement pair found here is a labelled counterpart too, and the audit's yield is
    66	  reported.
    67	- **The labels are frozen** (file and sha256) before Step 2's candidates are read.
    68	- **Pass:** a group holding a labelled counterpart is among the record's Step 2 candidates (`decisions.json` `candidates`) for at least 90
    69	  of 100 labelled records. Sampling stops at 100 labelled records. Fewer: **not measured**.
    70	
    71	**Line 2, clear wrong merges.**
    72	- **Population:** every repeat in `decisions.json` that was not refused, each joined to its recorded `repeat_of` original.
    73	- **Sample:** 200 at random.
    74	- **Reading:** the frozen Step 2 merge reading (`merge-prompt-1.md`, and `merge-third-prompt.md` on every pair either reader rejected).
    75	  The packet goes in the prompt in place of the file path.
    76	- **Pass:** the third reader's `wrong` count is at most 4 of 200. Fewer than 200 repeats: **not measured**.
    77	
    78	**Line 3, later details.**
    79	- **Population:** groups whose original has at least one later report.
    80	- **Sample:** 30 at random.
    81	- **The two renderings vary the grouping alone:**
    82	  - "apart": each member as its own entry;
    83	  - "grouped": the original, then each later report under it.
    84	  - Both use the same per-record fields (`step3/library.record_text`'s head line for every member).
    85	- **An independent detail key:** a third-family reader lists, from the members' own records, every material detail that only a later
    86	  report adds. This is the key, and it is frozen before either rendering is read.
    87	- **Reading:** two readers, one per family, each read both renderings under random labels and mark which key details each rendering
    88	  states.
    89	- **Pass:** over the 30 groups, the grouped rendering's paired detail total is no fewer than the apart rendering's, under both readers
    90	  (the recorded "no fewer" test). Fewer than 30 groups: **not measured**.
    91	
    92	The point estimate decides each line. A Wilson 95% interval is printed beside.
    93	
    94	## 3. D431's frozen-reference reading at 07-14 (printed beside; both systems)
    95	
    96	- **The as-of state:** each store's own readers at a day (`service.py`'s as-of path): questions opened from inputs published on or before
    97	  07-14, and the latest judgement with an input id of `day:2026-07-14` or earlier.
    98	- **The mapping:** two blind readers map each question to the 23 ruler questions under MATCHING-v2's SAME rule, and a third reader settles
    99	  disagreements.
   100	- **A substitution, recorded here before any output:**
   101	  - MATCHING-v2 §4's adapter, which re-asks the ruler question on the mapped evidence, is not built. It would change what the system
   102	    answered.
   103	  - This reading compares the answers actually given. It is therefore a different measurement from D395's seven-question score, and it
   104	    is labelled as such.
   105	- **Comparable only when the questions are the same:**
   106	  - a yes/no question with the same due day as the ruler question;
   107	  - a figure question with the same period, measure and unit. The unit comes from the old system's `view_keys.unit` and the new system's
   108	    checked ladder answer (`figure.unit`).
   109	  - Every other SAME match is "not comparable", for example another deadline or a part of a total.
   110	- **Agreement** uses `score_judgement.py`'s own rules.
   111	- **Printed:** per question and draw: agree, disagree, not comparable, not opened, or opened but not judged. Also the count of comparable
   112	  agreements on the seven graded questions, per draw and system.
   113	
   114	## 4. The floors (printed beside; proposed, not gates)
   115	
   116	From the cards, per system, under both countings:
   117	- **Coverage:** matters served / N.
   118	- **Trivia:** trivia marks among the guardrail sample's decided worth marks. Duplicates are reported apart.
   119	- **Supported:** supported answers among the guardrail sample's decided answers.
   120	
   121	Wrong citations and answer-changing omissions: **not measured**.
   122	
   123	## Tables
   124	
   125	**Value × reader:**
   126	
   127	| Value | Written by | Read by |
   128	|---|---|---|
   129	| `eligibility.json` (all fingerprints) | eligibility | every §1.6 tool, export, scorer |
   130	| d400 code check and reader lines | `d400_code_check`, Stage A tools | report: release status |
   131	| step2-lines.json | `step2_lines.py` | report: release status |
   132	| d431-0714.json | `d431_reading.py` | report |
   133	| beside quantities | `score_comparison.beside` | report |
   134	
   135	**State × event:**
   136	
   137	| Event | Handling |
   138	|---|---|
   139	| A reader session voids | Retried once, then reported missing. A line with a missing mark is not measured |
   140	| A draw stopped or ineligible | No release verdict. The tools run on what finished, as a diagnostic (plan §1.4 item 10) |
   141	| A file changed after eligibility | The tool refuses |
   142	| A component was redone | Its counted folder is the one `run.json` names |
     1	## Part A — Reading tools
     2	
     3	All six permitted `run.json` identities match. The native-ID sample, redo selection, prior-round debate, confirmed plants, split tally and the card’s own position in the opening order are fixed. I accept D675’s readings of the frozen rule. [Eligibility](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/eligibility.py:60) · [D675](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9729)
     4	
     5	- **The scorer still trusts the flags that decide which cards count.** It re-reads the key but compares only question IDs. In memory, changing six `guardrail` flags flipped a practical loss to a lead with every input file unchanged. Take `guardrail`, `covering` and answer type from the verified key. [Scorer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:158)
     6	- **Timing can pass with incomplete evidence.** A missing attempt log counts as zero attempts, and the writer can lose a log line after recording the charge. Reconcile settled attempts with ledger totals. Where timing cannot be established, report a diagnostic. [Eligibility](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/eligibility.py:70) · [Ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:101)
     7	- **Theme context still loses meaning.** The card drops the update marker and shows only the chosen condition. In two historical stores, 29 of 52 theme reasons cited another rung. Preserve the marker and show the numbered conditions those reasons refer to, without raw IDs. [Judge request](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:149) · [Card builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/build_cards.py:89)
     8	
     9	NOT READY: verify scoring flags and attempt-log completeness, and render the theme references.
    10	
    11	## Part B — §1.6 design
    12	
    13	- **D400 and Step 2 line 2 have usable inputs.** Run the D400 collector per draw because it reads one ladder folder and its packet files. Treat a skipped ladder as unmeasured. For line 2, join each accepted repeat to its recorded `repeat_of` and retain the frozen third-reader rule. [D400 check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/d400_code_check.py:19) · [Collector](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/collect_readings.py:38) · [Repeat record](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2/compare.py:109)
    14	- **Line 1 needs independent labels.** Lexical and party searches provide independent candidates but can miss the same pairs the product misses. Restore the earlier generator-miss audit. Remove the merge prompt’s claim that each candidate was already filed as a repeat. Freeze the labels before checking product retrieval. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:27) · [Audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:39) · [Prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-step2-forward-2026-11-08/merge-prompt-1.md:3)
    15	- **Line 3 needs the paired dossier test.** Both renderers exist. Hold the surrounding dossier and independent detail key fixed, vary grouping alone, and compare paired detail totals. The proposed zero-loss rule is stricter than the recorded “no fewer” test. [Renderers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step3/library.py:135) · [Recorded test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:305)
    16	- **D431 needs a recorded method decision.** Use the stores’ existing as-of readers for July 14. The no-adapter comparison can report agreement on the answers actually given, but D395’s seven-question score used ruler wording and ladders. Record the substitution and freeze comparability rules before reading. [As-of readers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:118) · [D395](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4303)
    17	- **Keep the verdict and release status separate.** “Practical lead” can coexist with “no release: hard check.” The floors can be computed from the cards. Assign the remaining report items, including D428 limits, illustrative statistics and time to opening. [Plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md:219) · [Frozen report](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/verdict-rule.json:77)
    18	
    19	CHANGE: fix Step 2’s labels and paired test, record the D431 substitution, and complete the report wiring.
