     1	You are an independent reader for a hedge-fund research system. Read-only task: do not edit files or run model calls.
     2	
     3	Read PACKET. Each entry is a pair of evidence records about NVIDIA from two different news articles, "earlier" and "later", each with its summary, verbatim source passages, the article context around them, the original party, reporting speaker, tier, statement date, period and dates. Do not open any other file in that folder.
     4	
     5	Answer two separate questions from the passages and context, not only the summaries.
     6	
     7	Question 1, the relation of LATER to EARLIER:
     8	- "same_statement": LATER makes the same statement or gives the same figure as EARLIER (a retelling, another outlet reporting the same claim, the same party repeating it);
     9	- "revision": LATER is the same party's later version of that statement that changes it (a revised figure, guidance, forecast, plan or schedule), or an official confirming or denying that report;
    10	- "different_fact_same_matter": both concern the same story or matter, but LATER states a different fact or event (for example, an arrest and a later charge in one case; a company's general programme and one customer's own deal under it);
    11	- "same_quantity_other_party": the same quantity or event estimated or claimed by a different party;
    12	- "different": different matters;
    13	- "insufficient": the material does not let you decide.
    14	
    15	Question 2, independently: list each material fact in LATER that EARLIER does not contain (a figure, condition, party, date or qualification an analyst would want to keep), as short phrases; an empty list if none. Then say whether merging LATER into EARLIER by keeping only EARLIER's text plus LATER's source would lose any of them ("source_only_merge_loses": true or false).
    16	
    17	Return only a JSON array in packet order: [{"id": "V..", "relation": "...", "added_material": ["..."], "source_only_merge_loses": true|false, "why": "<one short sentence>"}].
     6	## 1. The matching rule (an addition to the measurement; no frozen file changes)
     7	
     8	An opened question is the same as a ruler question when the same reported figure or event settles both (D248 and its boundaries).
     9	**Extra wording that does not separate them:**
    10	- a part, programme or single deal of a reference total (D248 boundary 1; R2-e);
    11	- the same event under another deadline, in either direction (boundary 2);
    12	- a later milestone, variant or parenthetical widening that the question's own check does not rest on (boundary 3; R2-f for steps of
    13	  one approval process).
    14	
    15	**It stays apart only when:**
    16	- it is a yes/no signing question beside an amount question (the Ohio exception, D248); or
    17	- its extra scope is its own check and could resolve on its own, as a separately watched bet.
    18	
    19	**How the rule was set** (`reader-brief.md`):
    20	- Two blind readers, Codex and Claude, read the 28 questions opened by the three stored unseeded c8 dev runs.
    21	- They agreed on SAME or not SAME for 24 of 28.
    22	- A third reader decided the 4 disagreements against the full texts and the decisions: all SAME (`adjudication.md`). The rule above is
    23	  that reader's general statement.
    24	- **Limit:** boundary 2 (another deadline) applies to an event's date, not to an amount held at a date. dev-d1 clean-1 asks for credit
    25	  support at end-2027, while q09 asks for a broader total at FY2027 year-end. The amounts can differ, so it is NOT SAME, as both readers
    26	  had it. dev-d2 and dev-d3 clean-1 are checked in the same FY2027 10-K and stay SAME.
    27	
    74	  - three draws.
    75	
    76	## 4. What a paid run needs first (none of it built yet)
    77	
    78	- **The adapter extension.** All 22 seed views plus q23 are created with their ruler text and ladder, so the frozen scorer accepts the
    79	  run. Each clean thesis mapped SAME by the rule above, as applied by an independent reader to the run's opened questions before any
    80	  judging, feeds its links to that view. Unmapped ruler questions have no evidence and are not judged.
    81	- **A council read and tests with mutants.**
    82	- **Cost:** about $7–8 (three clean draws at about $2.3; no new control, since the seeded Stage 2 is the comparison).

