## Part A — Reading tools

- **Scorer fixed.** The verified deck key now governs `guardrail`, `covering` and `type`. I changed each field independently in memory. All three changes were refused. [Scorer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:175)
- **Attempt-log check fixed.** It checks line count, total charges and outstanding reservations. My in-memory check rejected missing and short logs and accepted a reconciled log. [Eligibility](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/eligibility.py:70)
- **Theme context fixed.** Across both historical stores, all 52 themes showed numbered answer choices and all 18 update markers were preserved. I opened no live outputs. [Card renderer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/build_cards.py:156)

READY TO READ

## Part B — §1.6 design

- **D400 and release status.** I agree that an unmeasured D400 code check cannot clear release under the existing accounting minima. Record that interpretation. Use “hard checks clear” when they pass. Release still requires a practical lead and Alex’s word. The per-draw reader tools are usable. The code check still needs the designed skipped-ladder handling and fingerprinted inputs. [Accounting](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/accounting.py:198) · [D400 tool](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/d400_code_check.py:19) · [D665](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9425)
- **Step 2 lines 1 and 2 are buildable.** The trace and library support independent labelling and the `repeat_of` join. Keep line 1 labelled as recall over known counterparts. Five random pairs per record are a spot check. Restore the whole-history summary scan on a fixed stratified subset for the generator-miss audit. Line 2’s threshold and third-reader rule match the record. [Trace and library](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2/run_forward.py:116) · [Recorded audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:56) · [Recorded results](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:305)
- **Step 2 line 3 must exercise the shipped renderer.** The proposed common header adds fields the grouped output omits, which could mask a loss. Pair the actual `group_text` output with the ungrouped dossier using the same independent detail key. Use a paired interval over groups for the detail difference. Wilson fits the proportion lines. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:78) · [Renderers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step3/library.py:135)
- **D431 is buildable as the recorded as-run substitute.** Use `state_as_of` and borrow the frozen comparison rules. The scorer itself refuses unseeded stores. Join clean units by `clean_ladders.view_id`, including split children. Freeze how multiple matches and nonbinary rungs are handled before reading. [As-of reader](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:118) · [Frozen scorer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/score_judgement.py:36) · [Writer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/ladder_adapter.py:374)
- **The remaining report quantities have sources.** Label the Wilson interval as the share among discordant matters. Add D428’s last-judgement limit beside its figure and yes/no limits, with its original denominator. [Design table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:28) · [D428](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4761)

CHANGE: finish the input and release-status wiring, restore the search audit, use the shipped dossier renderer, and pin D431 comparability and the D428 report.
